The attached image details the active transport and cellular distribution of Nano-11 nanoparticles in the draining lymph nodes over time, crucial for its adjuvant properties. Flow cytometry analysis shows that Nano-11-containing cells peaked in number in the draining lymph node at day 2 post-injection. The majority (60-80%) of Nano-11 was consistently found within migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) from day 1 to day 7, with these cells also exhibiting significantly higher mean fluorescence intensity of Nano-11 per cell compared to other myeloid cell types. This indicates efficient uptake and targeting of Nano-11, and thus adsorbed antigens, to highly immunopotentiating MigDCs.